{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/tours\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/hamiltonianpath()"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/hamiltonianPath()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"method","role":"symbol","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P5ToursE15hamiltonianPath5Walks0F0Vy6VertexQz5Edges_5IndexQZGSgyF","modules":[{"name":"Tours","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"title":"hamiltonianPath()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"hamiltonianPath"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Walks4PathV","text":"Path"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P5EdgesQa","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":">?"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Method","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","remoteSource":{"fileName":"Hamiltonian.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Tours\/Hamiltonian.swift#L490"}},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A Hamiltonian path, or nil when there is none (or no vertex): the first one a depth-first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"backtracking search finds, from each vertex in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order, extending through each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"outEdges"},{"type":"text","text":" in order to an unvisited vertex. Self-loops never help; one vertex is the trivial path. Pruning cuts only subtrees with no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"solution (an unvisited vertex unreachable, or left without a usable predecessor or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"successor), so it keeps the order. Without a start the search is run again from each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex in turn until one succeeds, so a graph with no Hamiltonian path costs n searches."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours","doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"hamiltonianPath","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Path","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Walks4PathV","identifier":"doc:\/\/Walks\/documentation\/Walks\/Path"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertex"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P5EdgesQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"text":">?","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Exponential in the worst case (n! paths); O(degree) per step of the search,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"plus O(n + m) for the reachability test where it can fail (not after a step from a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex with no other unvisited successor, so a path or cycle graph takes O(n + m))."}]}],"type":"aside","name":"Complexity","style":"note"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://Tours/documentation/Tours/GraphProtocols":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"title":"GraphProtocols","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols","url":"\/documentation\/tours\/graphprotocols","role":"collection","type":"topic"},"doc://Tours/documentation/Tours/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph/hamiltonianPath()":{"url":"\/documentation\/tours\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/hamiltonianpath()","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/hamiltonianPath()","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"hamiltonianPath"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:5Walks4PathV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Path"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":">?"}],"title":"hamiltonianPath()","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A Hamiltonian path, or nil when there is none (or no vertex): the first one a depth-first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"backtracking search finds, from each vertex in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order, extending through each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"outEdges"},{"type":"text","text":" in order to an unvisited vertex. Self-loops never help; one vertex is the trivial path. Pruning cuts only subtrees with no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"solution (an unvisited vertex unreachable, or left without a usable predecessor or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"successor), so it keeps the order. Without a start the search is run again from each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex in turn until one succeeds, so a graph with no Hamiltonian path costs n searches."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Tours/documentation/Tours":{"type":"topic","title":"Tours","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/tours","role":"collection","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Tours/documentation/Tours/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"extension"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P","text":"DirectedGraph"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"title":"DirectedGraph","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","url":"\/documentation\/tours\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedGraph"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph/Vertex":{"type":"topic","title":"Vertex","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertex","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"associatedtype"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","text":"Hashable"}],"abstract":[],